    {
      "title": "Trump says he was ‘only kidding’ about making UFC’s Dana White next press secretary",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/08/trump-dana-white-press-secretary",
      "description": "<p>President says it was ‘just a little fun’ to picture White, UFC boss and Trump’s friend, in briefing room with fighters</p><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump\">Donald Trump</a> said on Sunday that he “was only kidding” when <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/07/donald-trump-dana-white-press-secretary\">he announced</a> a day earlier that he had offered the job of White House press secretary to Dana White, the chief executive of the Ultimate Fighting Championship (<a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/ufc\">UFC</a>).</p><p>Speaking to reporters on his way back the White House from his beach club in Florida, Trump explained the premise of his joke, that if the UFC boss, who is a devoted fan of the president, took over the briefing room, flanked by six fighters, reporters “wouldn’t mess around with him so much”.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/08/trump-dana-white-press-secretary\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-09T01:10:55"
    },
    {
      "title": "Why Trump joked about having Dana White as his White House press secretary",
      "link": "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/11/8/why-trump-wants-ufc-chief-dana-white-as-his-new-white-house-press-secretary?traffic_source=rss",
      "description": "The two have business ties going back decades, and White has helped Trump reach out to younger voters.",
